Cloudflare dynamic DNS client for multi-WAN setups.

Every entry is bound to an interface. The public address is taken from the
interface itself (e.g. PPPoE with a public IP) or queried from a check service
using the interface address as source. A policy routing rule (route-to) makes
sure the check request actually leaves through that interface's gateway, so
each WAN reports its own public IP instead of the one of the default route.

Records are updated via the Cloudflare API (API token), several interfaces can
maintain the same hostname (round robin), records are tagged via their comment.

